  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 1220 AM CDT Wed Sep 2 2026\n\nExtended Heat:\n\nGlobal models and ensembles show little to no indication in the\nridge--and the heat--breaking down anytime soon. In fact, the\nECMWF Extreme Forecast Index depicts widespread values of 0.8 to\n1.0 for MaxT but a Shift of Tails of 0, suggesting high\nconfidence in an abnormally hot but not extreme event. Indeed,\nNBM interquartile temperatures demonstrate small (2-4)\nvariability through the weekend. As a result, daily heat index\nvalues in the 100 to 105 degree range will continue, and the\nHeat Advisory remains in effect through Saturday. Further\nextension may be necessary in future forecast updates as\nconfidence increases. \n\nLimited Rain Chances:\n\nThe ridge and weak upper-level flow will largely keep rain\nchances to a minimum through the long term period. Analysis of\nensemble postage stamps depicts a limited number of members\nproducing scattered QPF footprints somewhere across the region\nSaturday through Monday as a diffuse cold front dips into\nMissouri. A lack of strong forcing limits confidence in this QPF\nbeing realized, however, and NBM PoPs remain limited to 10-20%.\n\nWith the persistent heat and a lack of appreciable rainfall,\ndrought conditions will deteriorate, and fuels will be more\nsusceptible to fire starts. These conditions will need to be\nmonitored closely in the coming weeks for the potential of\nworsening impacts. To that end, the CPC 6-1 Day Outlook depicts\na 70-80% chance of above-average temperatures continuing through\nthe September 7-11 period.",
